th both text and bio components and a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract introduces GEMGen, a large language model that generates small molecules from transcriptomic text representations, satisfying a generative architecture. It also notes training on large‑scale chemical perturbation data and transferable modeling across platforms, indicating foundation‑model characteristics.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract presents GEMGen, a new LLM‑based framework that maps text‑based gene‑set representations of transcriptomic phenotypes to generated small‑molecule structures, indicating a primary multimodal generative model with both biological and text components. | The abstract introduces GEMGen, a large language model that generates small molecules from transcriptomic representations, indicating a generative decoder architecture, and notes training on large‑scale data with transferable modeling across platforms, evidencing foundation‑model characteristics.",text_component_boundary;generative_boundary;biological_token_only
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:40:1961,Rethinking Genomic Modeling Through Optical Character Recognition,stable_include,UNCERTAIN|EXCLUDE|INCLUDE|INCLUDE|EXCLUDE,UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,OCR-capable vision-language model with document decoder and prompt-conditioned objectives,vision-language model processing DNA visual layouts,masked span completion and prompt-conditioned objectives,"Abstract presents OpticalDNA as a vision-language model for genomic modeling with masked span completion, but does not clearly describe natural-language text input or text-bio alignment, leaving text component and bridge uncertain.",EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,clear_exclude,none,none,masked span completion,"OpticalDNA uses a vision-language model on visual DNA layouts but does not describe natural-language text input or output; text component absent, leading to exclusion under EC2_no_text_component.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"OpticalDNA is a primary model paper that uses a vision-language model with a document decoder and prompt conditioning, making text and text-bio bridge central; DNA is the biological modality. | The abstract describes a novel vision-language model with a document decoder and masked span completion, indicating generative capability; it is compared to genomic foundation models and shows broad benchmark performance, suggesting foundation-model characteristics.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract presents OpticalDNA as a new vision‑language model for DNA that uses prompt‑conditioned objectives and a document decoder, indicating a substantive text component and a central text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents OpticalDNA with a visual encoder and a document decoder that performs masked span completion, indicating a generative decoder, and reports broad pretraining and strong performance across diverse genomic benchmarks, showing foundation‑model traits.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,,,,,"The paper