./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:25:- text_bio_bridge_present: yes | no | unclear
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:26:- primary_exclusion_code: review_editorial | benchmark_resource | application_wrapper | EC1_no_bio_modality | EC2_no_text_component | EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge | none
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:27:- uncertainty_reason: paper_type_unclear | bio_modality_unclear | text_component_unclear | text_bio_bridge_unclear | mixed_signals | none
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:29:- evidence_for_text_bio_bridge: short evidence phrase from the {{evidence_source}}, or none
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:30:- evidence_for_generative_model: not_assessed
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:31:- boundary_case: clear_include | wrapper_boundary | text_component_boundary | biological_token_only_boundary | generative_boundary | thin_abstract_boundary | clear_exclude | none
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:37:4. `text_bio_bridge_present`: Does the {{evidence_unit}} support a substantive text-bio bridge rather than a loose wrapper or side-feature use?
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:44:- If the record is review/editorial, benchmark/resource, or application_wrapper, set `paper_type` accordingly and use the matching exclusion code.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:45:- If a paper only uses embeddings, prompts, metadata descriptions, or outputs from an existing external LLM as side information for a downstream predictive bio task, treat it as `application_wrapper`, not as a substantive text-bio model.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:46:- Using an existing external LLM only to generate embeddings, labels, prompts, explanations, or text-derived features for a downstream classifier, risk model, annotation system, or predictor is `application_wrapper`, not a primary text-bio model.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:49:- A new method that merely attaches frozen/external LLM embeddings, prompts, labels, explanations, prototypes, or text-derived features to a downstream biological predictor is `application_wrapper` unless the {{evidence_unit}} presents the candidate model as a multimodal text-bio model, a bio-to-text/text-to-bio generator, or a generative model conditioned on text-derived evidence.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:50:- A paper that trains or fine-tunes a model to map biological data to natural-language descriptions, or natural-language prompts/descriptions to biological outputs, can satisfy `text_component_present=yes` and `text_bio_bridge_present=yes` if the {{evidence_unit}} makes that mapping central.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:51:- A paper that presents a new multimodal model or framework for generating natural-language descriptions from biological data, or generating biological outputs conditioned on natural-language/text-derived evidence, should not be labeled `application_wrapper` solely because it uses a pretrained LLM component.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:52:- Natural-language chat, question answering, dialogue, natural-language interfaces, or generated natural-language descriptions for biological data analysis are sufficient evidence for `text_bio_bridge_present=yes` when they are central to the candidate model.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:53:- Natural-language-derived priors, text summaries, report summaries, text descriptions, or text embeddings count as a text component and text-bio bridge when they condition, guide, or are cross-attended by the candidate generative model itself. They are not enough only when they are detached side features for a downstream classifier or predictor.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:61:- "uses GPT embeddings / LLM-derived gene embeddings / task-specific text prototypes for classification or prediction" -> `application_wrapper`, unless the abstract presents a central multimodal text-bio model or generator.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:62:- "gene tokens", "cell sentences", "DNA language", or "omics language model" with no natural-language text, prompt, caption, report, document, or explicit text-bio alignment -> `text_component_present=no`, `text_bio_bridge_present=no`.
./protocol/screening_prompt_templates/scope_reviewer_prompt.txt:65:- "diffusion/generative model conditioned on text summaries, text-derived priors, or natural-language descriptions" -> text component and text-bio bridge can be yes when the conditioning is part of the candidate model.
